RV64 already emits zero-extension instructions when verifier_zext is false.
Use that conservative JIT path to avoid the verifier's repeated array expansion
while loading large Capsule programs. Verification and CMPXCHG fixups remain
enabled. RV32 keeps its existing behavior.

--- a/arch/riscv/net/bpf_jit_core.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/net/bpf_jit_core.c
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 
 bool bpf_jit_needs_zext(void)
 {
-	return true;
+	return IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_32BIT);
 }
 
 struct bpf_prog *bpf_int_jit_compile(struct bpf_prog *prog)
